WEBVTT

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.160
In plays, there are hard scenes and fun scenes.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.120
In the same way,
we had our ups and downs, too.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:51.250
Team Otori's first performance together is...

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.200
...the second stage of Ayanagi Academy's
musical department entrance exam--

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.040
The Newcomers' Debut Performance!

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.040
"Formation A: Focus on rhythm" "Formation B: Go first, Move quickly"
"From A melody to top of B: Center, Pay attn to the line!"

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.910
Shall we begin, boys?

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.040
There's one week left before the performance.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.250
Your dancing is starting to look pretty good.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.370
So, I was thinking of adding
an arrangement to it today.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.750
An arrangement?

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.120
Yeah.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.660
Ever since that day, I've been thinking

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:22.620
about what magic to use to
make the prescribed story more fun.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.330
I'll show you the whole story right now.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.580
This is our new "Ayanagi Showtime"!

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.040
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:48.370
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:55.500
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:03.330
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.830
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:11.370
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:19.660
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:25.910
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:26.950
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:34.410
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.120
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:43.870
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.200
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.540
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.080
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.620
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.290
This is our "Ayanagi Showtime"...!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:17.080
Wow... I don't know how to
describe it... But it's interesting!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.080
I want to do this!

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.580
Well, it's not bad.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.540
We'll have to practice more than we have been.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.120
L-Let's do our best!

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.620
Yeah.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.910
Will two members of Team Otori please
come to the equipment room immediately?

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.410
Oh, we have to go get our costumes.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.750
Okay, we'll resume
practice in the afternoon then.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.700
Here are the costumes you requested.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.040
Please check them.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.830
Thank you!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.250
Huh? Are these it?

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.700
What the hell?!

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.200
There's no way I'm going on stage wearing this!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.500
But these were the only
costumes left. Right, Kuga?

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.750
It's because our leader kept
putting off requesting them.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.000
Tsukigami...

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.660
Costumes are part of an actor's body.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:21.000
You can't have a performance without them.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.620
N-Nayuki...

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.950
This is... probably your fault, Hoshitani...

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.700
Yeah...

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.450
Sorry guys...

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.500
But leave it to me.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.250
I didn't really want to use it...

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.370
But I'll use my last resort.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.950
L-Last resort?

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.500
Wh-Who are they?

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.700
It's worse than we'd heard.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.410
That's obvious.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.540
Your little sisters are twins, Nayuki?

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.410
This is Yuki and Tsumugi.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.750
They're both a little strange, but...

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.410
They're in junior high, right?

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.660
Can they sew?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:08.540
If we couldn't, we would not
come to such a squalid place,

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:11.580
even if our big brother asked us to!

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.200
It stinks of sweat.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.200
We only have one week. Will you make it?

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.290
Leave it to us!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.410
We'll make them better than
new in time for the performance!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.870
Naturally.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:27.790
But since they're so worn out,
won't you need to replace the fabric?

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.750
That's true. They'll pretty
much have to be remade.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.500
Of course.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.410
What about the design?
Don't tell me the girls will--?

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:37.830
Are you doubting our aesthetic sense?

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.160
How vexing.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.910
Even if you say that...

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.290
I've never seen anything you've made.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:48.290
If you're aiming to be an actor,
I'd want you to be more discerning than that.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.750
You're blind.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.870
Yuki, Tsumugi, that's enough.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.290
Jeez, they'd be cute if they didn't talk,
but they have bad personalities--

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.160
You!

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.410
If you're going to talk behind
our backs, do it so we can't hear!

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.540
How tiresome.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:02.660
Now, apologize!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.620
That means to say you're sorry.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.580
Sorry...

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.120
Tengenji...

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.250
...apologized!

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.200
Shut up! You're throwing off my groove!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.080
Tsumugi.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.000
Roger, Yuki.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.120
U-Um...

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:20.080
Don't move!

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.410
Freeze.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.540
Very well, we will take these costumes.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.910
It's crunch time.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.580
Thanks for your hard work.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.000
Team Otori...

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:53.370
Rumors are flying around the school
about how they'll definitely be cut, Hiragi.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.160
How is your team doing?

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:02.950
They might lose to your team, but they
have been consistently ranked near the top.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.500
I'm glad to hear that.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:12.410
However, if a prestigious Star Team
led by a Kao Council member fails...

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:16.540
...it could call into question the member's
qualifications to be in the Kao Council, right?

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.290
Of course, that is what would happen.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.580
One, two, three, four!

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.370
Was that good?

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.500
It's passing.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:35.620
All right!

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.700
Good job, Hoshitani!

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:42.500
Now you'll have to work hard so you can
do that during the real thing, too, you boor!

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.290
It's just as Tengenji says.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:48.000
The judges will be paying special
attention to the last formation.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.330
It must be perfect for the performance.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.620
But at this rate, I'm sure we'll pass!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.250
All right! Then, one more time!

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.120
Sorry, I have to go to my part-time job.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.160
What?!

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.370
I have to feed Tavian.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.830
O-Oh...

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.870
It's not good to get too into it.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.660
Don't worry about it, Hoshitani.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.750
"Debut performance!!"

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:35.790
"Second Round | Debut Performance"

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.950
All right. It's working.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.790
Come in.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:59.120
Do you have a minute?

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.250
Of course.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:06.160
There are unpleasant rumors circulating
about the Newcomers' Debut Performance...

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.500
Did you think I would be worried about them?

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.450
Do you have a plan up your sleeve?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.700
You make it sound so bad.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.910
I'm just planning on helping them pass.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.870
I do not know how you can be so confident,

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:27.950
but I do not want you to do anything that could
harm the tradition of Ayanagi Academy.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.580
That is all I came to say.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.330
I agree with you.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.790
Now, it's showtime.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:39.330
What?!

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.950
Our costumes aren't here yet?!

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.250
What happened with those twins?!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.080
When I talked to them on the phone yesterday,
they said they would make it in time...

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.370
It is time for the performance to begin.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.080
Performers, please gather at the hall.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:56.160
There's nothing we can do.
We'll just have to go for now!

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.330
We have no choice!

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.200
Sorry, everyone!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.120
The Newcomers' Debut Performance will now begin.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:14.500
This performance also serves as the second round
of the musical department entrance exam.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:19.450
Everyone, please give it
your all so you have no regrets.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.910
Yes, sir!

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.500
And now, we will determine
the performance order by lottery.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.580
Team leaders, please come forward.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.250
At least I have good luck with lotteries!

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.450
I'll get us the perfect spot near
the middle, so just leave it to me!

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.410
Sorry...

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.200
You sure have good luck with lotteries.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.040
Of all things, why did you have to get last?

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.370
The judging is relative. If we're last,
our mistakes will be more obvious.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:49.700
But our costumes aren't here yet, either,
so it might be better to be near the end...

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.330
That's a different problem.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.620
Oh, right. Let's look at today's fortune!

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:57.540
Look at mine!

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:01.120
Let's see... Hoshitani, your fortune today is...

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:01.910
"Libra - Today's Fortune: You will get
your friends involved with the worst results."

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:05.040
...you will get your friends
involved with the worst results...

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.450
Don't say such unlucky things!

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.370
Oh, but look at this!

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.160
"Libra: If you shake hands with
a friend, your luck will increase!!"

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.910
It says if you shake hands with
a friend, your luck will increase.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:17.410
Shake hands...

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.700
Tengenji!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:22.790
If I shake hands with you,
my luck will decrease.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:23.830
Uh, Tsukigami...!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:27.330
I don't believe in unscientific
things like fortunetelling.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:33.120
Hoshitani, you can shake hands with me?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:37.120
Next is Team Hiragi. Please get ready.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.250
Team Hiragi...

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.540
W-Wow...

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.040
It might be good that we're last...

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:05.290
The team that has to perform right
after them is probably at a disadvantage.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:08.660
But being last has its own pressure,
so Team Otori will have to stay <i>sharp</i> ...

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.700
...even if it's not <i>natural</i> .

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.410
Sorry, forget I said that.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.500
He's laughing...

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.950
I got nervous all of a sudden!

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.450
Now?

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.580
No one expects much of us, anyway.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:32.830
Just relax.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.830
You had to say it, huh?

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.910
But we won't let things end here, right?

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:40.410
It's like the rebellion of space junk.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:43.080
Don't call us junk.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.750
Space junk of the Star Teams...
It's like we're stardust...

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.290
That's pretty good!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:56.250
We should put on the best
performance we can in our own way!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.370
What you're saying is true, but...

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.870
You shouldn't talk.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.660
Seriously.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.410
But I'm the leader...

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.080
We apologize for being late.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.250
We repent.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:12.950
To make up for it,
we've made the best costumes ever!

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.750
Patting ourselves on the back.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.750
These are the same as those...?

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:20.160
They look completely different!

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.830
They're avant-garde!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.950
They seem fitting for Team Otori.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:27.200
Ah, I'm really nervous now!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.120
Yuki.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.500
Right, Tsumugi.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:31.370
"Secret recipe"

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.830
Oh, that's--!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.620
S-Stop it...!

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.370
N-Nayuki?!

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:46.290
It's a tea that eases nervousness
handed down in the Nayuki family!

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:47.620
It's a secret recipe.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.000
I suppose we could let you have a cup, though.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.370
It's high quality.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.790
No, thank you!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.500
You're almost on. Please get ready.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.080
R-Right!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.830
Hoshitani.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.620
Let's do the last formation carefully.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.450
Feel the rest of us around you.

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.750
We'll match what you do, leader.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.250
Thanks.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:28.450
The five of us are a team.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.200
We can do it.

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.950
Let's have fun with this stardust rebellion!

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:36.000
Yeah!

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.500
Let's have a great performance!

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:43.120
A great performance!

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.370
Now, boys! It's time to play!

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.950
♪ I am going on a journey now ♪

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.080
♪ Unfolding the map of old ♪

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:15.500
♪ I am going on a journey now ♪

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.750
♪ Come, let's begin the adventure ♪

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:25.620
♪ I cannot predict what will happen ♪

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:33.200
♪ Who will I meet? My heart flies away on wings ♪

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:40.000
♪ In the fantasy garden with the azure fountain ♪

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.080
♪ It blooms only once in a thousand years... ♪

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:48.540
♪ ...this mysterious flower ♪

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:49.330
♪ Go forward! ♪

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:56.040
♪ Continuing the journey far, far away ♪

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:02.790
♪ I will never be afraid of being lonely ♪

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:09.620
♪ Heading for the sun far, far away ♪

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:16.370
♪ A journey to find my true self ♪

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.200
♪ Youth! ♪

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:24.290
♪ It's a brightly shining dream! ♪

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.950
This is...

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.290
What is this?

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:49.290
You call this "Ayanagi Showtime"?!

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:52.120
There's no way we can accept this!

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.700
Are you sure about that?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:59.200
It's true that the Newcomers'
Debut Performance specifies that

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.370
everyone must perform "Ayanagi Showtime."

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:07.540
But what is required is to include
the prescribed steps and sequences.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.870
There is no stipulation
as to how it is arranged.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:14.080
Wanna take a look at the rulebook
for the Newcomers' Debut Performance?

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.700
While honoring the school's tradition,

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:22.000
we imitated the original "Ayanagi Showtime"
from the founding of the school,

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.410
but that became nothing more than a name.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:30.700
Following the founding ideology of Ayanagi
Academy that honored freedom of expression,

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:34.200
we presented a new
"Ayanagi Showtime" for you to watch.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.830
Do you think that kind of
sophistry will work here, Otori?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:43.330
Unfortunately, you don't have
the right to denounce us, Akatsuki.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.910
What did you say?!

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:46.250
Hiragi!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.830
As long as they have not
broken the rules, I cannot stop it.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:54.580
But this desecrates the
tradition of Ayanagi Academy!

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:59.910
Akatsuki, honoring the rules is
also a tradition of Ayanagi Academy.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.580
Hiragi...

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.330
What is all this commotion?

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.330
That was amazing, Team Otori!

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:17.500
That was great!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.540
I'd never seen
"Ayanagi Showtime" like this before!

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.580
I was kind of moved!

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.540
Did you plan this?

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:35.450
Who knows? But isn't it fine
since people seem excited about it?

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.700
Hmph, that's just a stunt.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:48.040
But I'm drawn to it for some reason.
What do you think, Eigo?

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:50.660
It's an interesting way of doing things.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.910
Those guys are great!

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:55.830
That Shu really did it, huh?

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:07.080
The results of the judging of the Newcomers'
Debut Performance will now be posted.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:14.200
We just have to be in the top ten...!

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:15.580
Here it is!

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.040
"Rank | Team Name"
"1. Team Hiragi" "2. Team Akatsuki" "3. Team Sazanami"

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:27.040
"4. Team Yuzuriha" "5. Team F" "6. Team B"

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.330
"7. Team G" "8. Team Otori" "9. Team A"

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.330
There! We're 8th!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.790
We made it!

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.450
Of course!

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.660
All right!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.250
This has to be some kind of mistake.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.750
Yes!

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:02.250
What did you think of my students?

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:07.660
See? I told you they'd pass.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:10.410
I suppose I should say, "Congratulations."

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:13.620
Those guys are pretty fun, don't you think?

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:18.250
I have never evaluated actors
based on whether or not they were fun.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.080
What I am concerned about is Ayanagi--

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:25.160
...is if they are worthy to be put out
into the world as Ayanagi musical actors.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.750
Right?

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:33.290
Sorry, but I don't want to restrict my students.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.540
What flavor does their singing have?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.620
Is their dancing hot or cold?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:42.080
Acting is something so vivid
it can bring people to tears.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.830
I want to teach them to
perform that kind of musical.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.910
That's why you never change.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:53.120
You haven't changed one bit since that time!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.000
There was once a time when you
were a member of Team Tsukigami,

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:00.410
and we chased the same
dream in the same Star Team.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.120
However--

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.580
You left. You ran away!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:15.080
You haven't changed at all
since that time you left me.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.500
You haven't changed, either.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:20.700
The same blood flows in our veins.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.040
Tsubasa...

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:32.040
Even if we have the same blood,
you and I are different...

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.580
...Big Brother.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:58.410
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:04.910
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:08.410
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:12.700
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:16.830
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:20.120
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:23.660
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:27.660
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:30.830
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:34.700
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:38.200
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:41.950
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:45.500
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:49.160
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:55.160
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.950
Cheers!

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:13.330
I would've been a goner if Tengenji
and Tsukigami hadn't grabbed my hands.

00:23:13.330 --> 00:23:16.330
Just like the fortune said,
shaking hands brought good luck, huh?

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.250
Oh, you're right! That's amazing!

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:24.410
It was really fun thanks to you guys.

00:23:24.410 --> 00:23:26.410
We're the best team ever!

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:29.870
Well, but we can't really count on our leader.

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:32.830
He messes up at important times.

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:34.330
He needs to reflect on his actions.

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:36.500
Um...

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:40.040
As a punishment, let's make
him drink Nayuki's family tea.

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:43.540
There was the matter of the costumes, too.
Two cups seems reasonable.

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:46.950
If we make him drink it whenever
he messes up, he might improve faster.

00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:51.370
Oh, then I'll have my sisters prepare some.

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:53.330
Give me a break!

00:23:55.370 --> 00:24:19.750
"Act 7"

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:57.870
Mr. Otori!

00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.450
What is it, girls?

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:03.950
Why wasn't our brother in the
center for the debut performance?

00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:06.410
Certain death.

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.200
Amazing!

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:19.750
"Hope you'll watch next 
week, too. Right, Eigo?"
